227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (My friends are announcing their new beginnings, their rooms already stripping down to bare walls and forgotten posters. Watching them is like watching a film strip unspooling in reverse, everything is suddenly raw and exposed. There is the laughter, the promises to call, the casual jokes about "the real world" that feel heavy with subtext. We are standing on the precipice of adulthood, and I find myself clinging to the banality of our shared teenage years: the lunch breaks, the science lab conversations, the way we knew exactly who each other was before the world decided who we ought to be.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (And then, the fear sets in. It isn't just about the grades anymore, or the transcripts, or the daunting weight of the university applications sitting on my desk. It is the fear of fragmentation. I worry that if I step out of this defined space, this high school ecosystem that has nurtured and bruised me in equal measure, I will cease to be the person I have become. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E ( am terrified that the versions of us that exist in the safety of these hallways will be diluted by the distance and new schedules. I am afraid of the "what comes next," because "what comes next" means I am no longer a student in the safe, predictable sense. I am becoming someone who has to define themselves, without the crutch of a bell schedule.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Yet, standing in the driveway as the tail lights fade, or, in my case, sitting in the quiet of my bedroom as the last email is sent, I am trying to remember that this isn't an ending. It is a metamorphosis.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Charlie saw the tunnel lights and felt the rush of existing in a singular, perfect moment. Maybe that is the trick to post-exam therapy. We have to stop looking at the future as a cliff we are about to fall off of, and start looking at it as the wind we are about to fly through.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (We are exhausted, yes. We are grieving a version of ourselves that is fading away, that much is true. But we are also standing at the threshold of something vast. The terror of the unknown is just another way of saying that the possibilities are endless. We are not just the sum of our grades or the titles we hold. We are the memories we keep, the people we have loved, and the potential we carry into the dark.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (In the quiet of this new, terrifying freedom, I am choosing to believe the truth of it: We are infinite.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
