/P 145 0 R
/E (Academic retribution. A price all must pay for the pursuit of knowledge, more suitably, paid by those surviving in a nation that grows on the dreams of yearners. Its attainment is no play for the weak. It is a constant fight against obedience, corruption and the will to end it all; an excruciating pain birthed inside all who challenge such vile system. It is the reason for aggression and chaos.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
239 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (A vessel lies, defeated, on a cold bed, as the darkness around it covers every inch of its existence. It lays, ruined. Overwhelmed. Alone. There is no light in its thoughts. Only despair and terror, consuming every blissful future.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (It lies: aggrieved. Hopeless. No comfort. No warmth. Waiting for death to come and sit beside it; bestowing the gift of liberation. Freedom. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (An escape from all horrors it has been bear to, and the ones yet to come. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (But in all this, the moon shines through the shattered glass pane. As the cracks illustrate light in bizarre patterns, aiding the vessel to perceive, that death is most certain, but life does not necessarily need to be lived in vain.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
