248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (The vessel is not some ambiguous entity. It is not foreign. It is us. It is the depiction of our reality and feelings. A shadow of our mind; as we wait for all troubles to pass with time, hoping to stop at a satisfying end. We desire for all that we want to achieve, to be as easy as the sound of pain: as with much haste it comes and with greatness it inflicts.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (We want to experience, attain and enjoy all what we can and cannot achieve. We want it all, not through sacrifice, but through happiness. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (Through freedom. By choice. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (But is it not, that the foundational rules of this world constitute sacrifice. Anguish. Harm? How can we be without being criticized, and humiliated? Without being trapped and ceased of our decisions.)
