/P 161 0 R
/E (There are countless reasons for such aggreivance. Most abundantly: a man, eaten by his bitter loneliness targeting a virgin for his desires; perhaps a brother who has sought as his sister to be an object to violate and harm, releasing his frustration; perhaps a father who failed to protect his daughter's dignity as to being feared by the societies' disgusting and utmost vile criticism; or a husband who failed to save his wife from the pressure by his family, a family that always swore to love him, but failed when needed to. Or perhaps it was a young boy, being granted every wish he dreamt regardless of his doubtful character, his wish to hurt others or to suppress the voices of the innocent. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (Or maybe, it was in fact a woman's fault. A woman who had the utmost desire to express herself, her personality and her life. A woman who wanted to experience freedom without bounds. A woman who wanted to roam free on God's earth. It was inevitably her fault for having to dreamt such fantasies. It was her fault for being oblivious; failing to acknowledge that this can never be true. Not as long as a man fails to respect himself. For a man who fails to protect his own identity inflicts pain onto another, and what most indication of his manhood is, than to insult and affect a woman.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
