/P 166 0 R
/E (So that's exactly what I did. I called the same friend and we met at the Quaid-e-Azam House Museum. The beautiful house was filled with countless pieces of Quaid-e-Azam and Fatima Jinnah's life. The cane Jinnah used, the table they had meals at, their cars, Fatima Jinnah's makeup powder case, her vanity, and even Quaid-e-Azam's cigar box were kept there. Once again I felt like an intruder looking into an intimate part of someone's life. Even more shocking, this time the entire tour cost us zero rupees, and we even had a tour guide who had so much knowledge about the place.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
